    "notes": {
        "40eb182d-a367-497f-82ba-6c162f8e72c4": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": -272,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThe SetVariable **projectId** must be the ID of a Google Cloud project the connected account can create buckets in (billing enabled, Cloud Storage JSON API enabled). The flows create their own buckets (`e2e-gcs-…`) in that project and delete them at the end. See artifacts/test-flows/README.md.\n\nThe triggers are configured with the same project ID (**New Bucket**) and the bucket **appmixer-e2e-gcs-trigger** (**New or Updated Object**, prefix `e2e-trigger/`): create that bucket once in the project."
        },
        "587b29b4-e73e-49cc-b700-7e97fff39626": {
            "x": 800,
            "y": -272,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⏱ Timing\n\nThe Wait lets both polling triggers record their baseline on the first tick: a bucket or an object created before that is never reported. Do not remove it. Do not run this flow in parallel with the other Cloud Storage flows in the same project: New Bucket would also see their buckets."
        }
    }
